========================================================================
DATA AVAILABILITY AND SOURCE CORRESPONDENCE STATEMENT
Project: Sleep Deprivation Meta-analysis (Cross-Platform Transcriptomics)
========================================================================

1. PUBLIC REPOSITORY REQUISITION
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The raw transcriptomic sequencing data and microarray intensity assets 
synthesized in this study are publicly available and were retrieved from 
the National Center for Biotechnology Information (NCBI) Gene Expression 
Omnibus (GEO) database (https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/).

2. SPECIFIC ACCESSION CORRESPONDENCE
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The individual datasets utilized within this meta-analysis framework 
correspond exactly to the cohort profiles mapped in the manuscript text:

  - Microarray Cohorts (Table 2) : GSE6514, GSE33302
  - RNA-seq Cohorts (Table 3)    : GSE132074, GSE144957, GSE222410, 
                                   GSE113754, GSE211088, GSE211301, 
                                   GSE156925, GSE166831

3. LOCAL REPOSITORY EXCLUSIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Due to file size and storage threshold considerations within public code 
repositories, raw binary array intensities (.CEL files), raw FASTQ sequence 
reads (.fastq.gz), and intermediate aligned BAM files are excluded from this 
local GitHub directory. 

4. PIPELINE REPRODUCIBILITY CONSTRAINTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Full end-to-end exact pipeline replication can be executed seamlessly by:
  1. Programmatically downloading the target dataset matrices from the 
     NCBI GEO database using the accessions listed above.
  2. Placing the source files into their designated subdirectories 
     under the local 'data/' directory.
  3. Running the sequential script stack (01 to 08) provided within 
     the 'script/' directory of this repository.

For further metadata clarifications, structural target annotations, or 
phenotype mapping assistance, please consult the manuscript's Supplementary 
Tables or open an issue directly in this repository.

